## Open items

### 1. Social feed is running on a fallback, not on Facebook/X
Henry must create the credentials himself — X needs a paid API plan and Facebook
needs an app review, both tied to his identity. **Do not attempt to register
developer accounts on his behalf.**

Until then both regions fall back to the keyless public StockTwits stream, which
does collect real data (first prod cycle: 150 posts across the top-5). Adding
`X_BEARER_TOKEN` or `FACEBOOK_ACCESS_TOKEN` + `SOCIAL_FACEBOOK_PAGES` to
`~/sooppiy/.env` flips that region to its primary automatically — no code change.
`SOCIAL_KEYLESS_FALLBACK=false` disables the fallback.

### 2. Run auto-restart — DESIGN DECISION PENDING, do not build yet
Henry asked: when a run stops, automatically create a new one with the same
settings. He was asked to choose a scope and **dismissed the question**, so it is
unresolved. Do not implement on a guess — two of the three readings silently
disable protections he already has:

- Goal-reached stops (`profit_target`, `max_trades`, `at_time`) — safe to restart
- Protective stops (`max_loss`, `synthetic_liquidation`, `stop_eval_failed`,
  errors) — restarting re-enters the same losing setup and turns his max-loss
  into a repeating loss
- `user_stop` — restarting makes the Stop button useless; the run resurrects

Stop reasons are produced by `_evaluate_stop` in `service/server/run_engine.py`.

### 3. AutomationPage sends a stale agent token (pre-existing, real)
`service/frontend/src/pages/AutomationPage.tsx` captures the claw token once at
mount with a **setter-less** `useState`. `App` rotates the agent token
(`linkAgent`, and the 401 re-link path), after which that page keeps sending the
old value and its own calls — the rules list — 401 **silently**, rendering as an
empty page rather than an error. `MonitorPage` is immune because `App` passes it
a live token prop.

Deliberately left unfixed so a bug fix was not smuggled into a revert. Fix =
give the state a setter and sync it (focus + `storage` event + short interval).

