## Things that will bite you

**Verify behaviour, not labels.** A page whose every API call 401s still renders
all its section headings. Checking that headings appear "passed" a completely
unusable page in this session. Assert on real values, or read the network.

**The SPA catch-all used to swallow `/api/*`.** Fixed in `ade4e53`, but older
smoke checks that curl'd a wrong API path and got `200` were measuring the HTML
fallback, not the API. `/api/leaderboard` 404 is correct — it was never a route.

**Publish the SPA separately.** Host nginx serves `/usr/share/nginx/sooppiy`;
building the image is not enough for a frontend change, and you must
`sudo restorecon -R /usr/share/nginx/sooppiy` afterwards or SELinux 500s the site.

**Build the deploy package with `git archive`, never macOS `tar`** — bsdtar emits
AppleDouble `._*` files that corrupt sources under GNU tar. Check
`find /tmp/app-new -name "._*" | wc -l` = 0.

**Diff prod against main before replacing `app/`.** Other sessions deploy this
box; prod has been ahead of main before. md5-diff both trees and confirm every
differing file is one you touched.

Full procedure, hazards and rollback: see the deploy runbook in `docs/` and the
project memory `sooppiy-deploy-procedure`.

